cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the data products in it, please cite the repository, and cite the article once it is published."
title: "Competing risks in machine-learning cardiovascular risk prediction: analysis pipeline"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible pipeline for a paired-learner benchmark of naive and competing-risk
  survival models for 10-year cardiovascular mortality in NHANES 1999-2018 linked to
  the NCHS 2019 public-use Linked Mortality File, with the full calibration hierarchy,
  inverse-probability-of-censoring-weighted discrimination, competing-risk-consistent
  net benefit, and a closed-form decomposition of the naive-versus-competing difference.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-14"
license: MIT
